LOCATION:Shreve Auditorium
SUMMARY:CRRES Symposium: Venezuelan Politics in the Wake of Crisis
DESCRIPTION:Venezuelan Politics in the Wake of CrisisFriday\, October 2nd
 9:30a.m.-4:00p.m.Breakfast served at 9amHamilton Lugar School -Shreve Aud
 itoriumFor Schedule: Center for Research Race &amp\; Ethnicity in Society
 's Event Page (https://crres.indiana.edu/events/venezuela-symposium.html)
 &#160\;  Against the backdrop of political upheaval\, foreign interventio
 n\, natural disaster\, and long-standing infrastructure challenges\, Vene
 zuelan Politics in the Wake of Crisis will bring together scholars and a 
 human rights advocate for an interdisciplinary examination of contemporar
 y Venezuela.  The symposium will feature Verónica Zubillaga of the Unive
 rsity of Illinois Chicago and Yoletty Bracho of Avignon University\, join
 ing in person\; Magdalena López of the University of Notre Dame and the 
 University Institute of Lisbon\, joining virtually\; and Venezuelan attor
 ney and human rights advocate Venus Marina Faddoul Barrios\, director of 
 the NGO 100% Estrógeno\, joining virtually from Spain.  Drawing on exper
 tise in political participation\, urban and state violence\, cultural cri
 ticism\, human rights\, and gender justice\, the panelists will examine h
 ow Venezuela's continuing crises have affected political life\, civil soc
 iety\, migration and displacement\, and regional relations. The program w
 ill also include a screening of 22 de mayo (1969) by Cine Urgente moderat
 ed by Dr. Noraeden Mora from the Department of Spanish and Portuguese.  O
 rganized by the Center for Research on Race and Ethnicity in Society (CRR
 ES)\, in collaboration with the Center for Latin American and Caribbean S
 tudies (CLACS)\, the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International St
 udies (HLS)\, the Department of History\, and the Department of Spanish a
 nd Portuguese. Meeting URL: https://iu.zoom.us/j/89320581931?pwd=UjTCinQO
 mrBAwblMTkz06GLsl3eOZ4.1
